 # Pending inbox re-delivers already-handled messages after abort+resume
 
 Observed by Doug: on a long multi-turn session, a user-originated abort followed by a new user prompt dumps already-handled Tattler/Chorus messages back into context, and the agent reports it already processed them. Diagnosis: the pending-inbox read position (cursor) is not durably advanced through the abort+resume cycle, so before_agent_start re-drains an inbox it already drained. This is the inverse of the loss-direction abort bugs (TAT-37 et al.): over-delivery, not loss. Fix locus: durable-rooms v1 slice -- per-agent cursor in a SQLite cursors table, advanced on tool-call SUCCESS (atomicity boundary), so delivered-but-uncommitted messages re-deliver while committed ones never do. Resolved-by the durable Chorus room log + cursor slice; see .sandpiper/docs/specs/durable-rooms-sizing.md (chunk 3). Distinct from TAT-64/TAT-65 (render-delay).
 
